{"_data": [{"type": "metadata", "contents": [{"content": "Peter's Dating Misadventures", "type": "lesson_name"}, {"content": "Late, Again!", "type": "unit_name"}, {"content": 8, "type": "position"}, {"content": "stub", "type": "origin"}, {"content": 8, "type": "lesson"}, {"content": "B1.3", "type": "level"}]}, {"type": "achievment_test", "contents": [{"content": "false", "type": "test"}]}, {"type": "objectives", "contents": [{"content": "Describe complicated or unusual events in the past through a wider range of B1 language in both work and social contexts.", "type": "primary"}, {"content": "Writes well-organized texts or articles about explaining the rules and regulations in his/her industry using appropriate grammar, vocabulary, spelling coherence and cohesion, and different levels of formality. ", "type": "secondary_1"}, {"content": "Writes well-organized texts or articles about explaining the rules and regulations in his/her industry using appropriate grammar, vocabulary, spelling coherence and cohesion, and different levels of formality. ", "type": "secondary_2"}, {"content": "Writes well-organized texts or articles about explaining the rules and regulations in his/her industry using appropriate grammar, vocabulary, spelling coherence and cohesion, and different levels of formality. ", "type": "secondary_3"}, {"content": "Writes well-organized texts or articles about explaining the rules and regulations in his/her industry using appropriate grammar, vocabulary, spelling coherence and cohesion, and different levels of formality. ", "type": "secondary_4"}, {"content": "Writes well-organized texts or articles about explaining the rules and regulations in his/her industry using appropriate grammar, vocabulary, spelling coherence and cohesion, and different levels of formality. ", "type": "secondary_5"}, {"content": "Writes well-organized texts or articles about explaining the rules and regulations in his/her industry using appropriate grammar, vocabulary, spelling coherence and cohesion, and different levels of formality. ", "type": "secondary_6"}, {"content": "Writes well-organized texts or articles about explaining the rules and regulations in his/her industry using appropriate grammar, vocabulary, spelling coherence and cohesion, and different levels of formality. ", "type": "secondary_7"}, {"content": "Writes well-organized texts or articles about explaining the rules and regulations in his/her industry using appropriate grammar, vocabulary, spelling coherence and cohesion, and different levels of formality. ", "type": "secondary_8"}]}, {"content": "engenn8le08ob08re1img01.jpg", "type": "background_image"}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Expressing an Opinion About Past Events ", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " You use the Past Perfect tense to identify and talk about an 'earlier past'.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "When you are talking about a past event, you can refer to something that happened at an earlier time to that past event by using the Past Perfect tense.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "If I had waited for an hour and a half, there would not have been another date. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "We had thought they might not be ready but they are enjoying their new routine. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "I heard that the subway is delayed due to water on the tracks at Bloom Station. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "The structure of the Past Perfect is: <br> <span class=\"strong\">Subject + had + past participle</span>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"italic\">When I arrived at the party, Vanessa <span class=\"strong\">had</span> already <span class=\"strong\">gone</span> home</span>.<br> Which event happened <span class=\"italic\">first</span>? Vanessa went home.<br> Which event happened <span class=\"italic\">later</span>? I arrived at the party.<br>", "type": "text"}, {"content": "You use the Past Perfect tense (not Simple Past) when you want to talk about how long something had continued <span class=\"strong\">up to a past moment</span>. ", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "learning_points", "contents": [{"content": "Modals for Possibility and Certainty", "type": "heading"}, {"content": " You use modals when you want to express possibility, certainty, suggestions and expectations.", "type": "describer"}, {"content": "You use <span class=\"italic\">may</span>, <span class=\"italic\">might</span> and <span class=\"italic\">could</span> to express possibility in the past and in the future.<br /> *Might suggests that something is less possible than may.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "She must be trying to tell me something.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "She might be stuck in traffic. ", "type": "example"}, {"content": "might / might not + infinitive could / could not + infinitive may / may not + infinitive ", "type": "text"}, {"content": "<span class=\"strong\">Expressing Certainty:</span> You use <span class=\"strong\">must</span> to express that something is necessarily true. ", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "to saunter", "type": "name"}, {"content": "to walk along in a slow and relaxed manner", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(verb)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: The game had almost ended before she sauntered in.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le08ob08aud01", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word_describer", "contents": [{"content": " These are words you hear in a conversation between friends.", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "dating scene", "type": "name"}, {"content": " to visit different places when you are single", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Are you still on the dating scene?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le08ob08aud02", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "it's a zoo", "type": "name"}, {"content": "a wild, busy period", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: It's a zoo after work.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le08ob08aud03", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "track ", "type": "name"}, {"content": " iron rows that a train travels on", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: There was water flowing over the tracks.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le08ob08aud04", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "field ", "type": "name"}, {"content": "line of work", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(noun)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: She is in the same field.", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le08ob08aud05", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "target_word", "contents": [{"content": "big screen", "type": "name"}, {"content": " a large television ", "type": "definition"}, {"content": "(expression)", "type": "part_speech"}, {"content": "Example: Do you want to watch the game on the big screen?", "type": "example"}, {"content": "engenn8le08ob08aud06", "type": "audio"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_extension", "contents": [{"content": "Go online and compare the different manners and customs in two countries in different parts of the world.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Research how people greet each other, eat, and communicate differently.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Write brief notes on the similarities and differences.", "type": "text"}, {"content": "Use the notes to write a paragraph about the manners and customs in the two countries. Include a topic sentence, supporting sentences and a concluding sentence. <br/>For example: <span class=\"italic\">There are significant cultural differences between the United States and China. In China it is impolite to leave your shoes on when you enter a house.</span>", "type": "text"}]}, {"type": "takeaway_assessment"